1
00:00:03,208 --> 00:00:07,783
On the import page for a type, the upload requirements come first.

2
00:00:07,783 --> 00:00:12,168
Download template gives a file with every column already named.

3
00:00:12,168 --> 00:00:14,900
The ContentItemId column is optional.

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:18,840
Leave it empty to create an item, or fill it in with the

5
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:21,954
id of an existing item to update that item.

6
00:00:21,954 --> 00:00:25,068
The title is the only required column here.

7
00:00:25,519 --> 00:00:27,050
Parts come first.

8
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:30,779
The HTML body and the Markdown body take the text.

9
00:00:30,779 --> 00:00:34,574
The alias and the URL path take the item's address.

10
00:00:34,574 --> 00:00:39,235
The archive and publish dates schedule the item, and are in UTC.

11
00:00:39,235 --> 00:00:41,699
A Liquid part takes a template.

12
00:00:42,149 --> 00:00:46,902
Then the type's own fields, named after the part and the field.

13
00:00:46,902 --> 00:00:51,380
A text field takes text, and a number field takes a number.

14
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:54,686
Date and time fields take dates and times.

15
00:00:54,686 --> 00:00:57,579
A boolean field takes True or False.

16
00:00:58,030 --> 00:01:03,579
A multiple text field takes all its values in one cell, separated by a bar.

17
00:01:03,579 --> 00:01:07,004
A link has its URL, its text and its target.

18
00:01:07,004 --> 00:01:09,607
A YouTube field has its address.

19
00:01:09,607 --> 00:01:14,950
A content picker takes the ids of the items to link, separated by a bar.

